  "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼B(160,0.55),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(X\\le 95).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ | $\\,0.8599\\,$ | $\\,0.8621\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ | $\\,0.8830\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |",
